    "id": "p6-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A number is chosen from the first 15 positive whole numbers. What is the probability that it is exactly divisible by both 3 and 4?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{15}$",
      "worked": "The only number from 1 to 15 divisible by both 3 and 4 is 12. There is 1 favourable outcome among 15 equally likely outcomes.\n$$P(\\text{divisible by both 3 and 4})=\\frac{1}{15}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
